    <heading level="1">Extensions</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find the area of the ellipse. The area of an ellipse is given by the formula $$\text{Area} = a \cdot b \cdot \pi.$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="57" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{\left( {x - 3} \right)^{2}}{9} + \frac{\left( {y - 3} \right)^{2}}{16} = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$Area = 12\pi squareunits Area = 12\pi squareunits$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
